  "notes": "Free self-serve access: any Asana user can generate a Personal Access Token from the developer console (app.asana.com/0/my-apps) with no paid plan or approval required, and PATs are passed as Bearer tokens. OAuth2 is the recommended method for multi-user apps and is also what the official MCP server (V2, launched Feb 2026) uses. A separate Service Account auth method exists but is Enterprise-tier/admin-only and is not counted here since PAT/OAuth already provide self-serve access. API is REST, ~167 endpoints per OpenAPI spec.",
